{"kind":"assert","text":"NF-5 ruling on 2a65dcff.\n\nQuestion 1. No deployed Worker has served the draft layout, so no\ncurrent-room data needs recovery. The fact: each deployed commit is\nan ancestor of main, and none holds `browser-custody.ts`. I checked\n64112e45, 5b342ee9, 7135dc39 and a76764a7 with `git ls-tree`. The\nplanner made each deployment, each from main. The draft ran only in\nthe profiles of your local harness.\n\nSo:\n- The layout with one row for each outcome position is the first\n  released layout. Write no conversion, no second version beside a\n  draft version, and no path that keeps the draft `segments` store.\n- A database whose layout the code does not know is unreadable. It\n  is never absent and never reset. Your fail-closed rule stays.\n- Choose a database name or a version that a draft profile cannot\n  pass for. Say which in the note.\n\nQuestion 2. Confirmed, each part:\n- `close` and `versionchange` retire the store instance for good. A\n  retired store refuses new work and queued work, and it closes a\n  connection that opens late.\n- A transaction in flight ends by its own result, and the custody\n  bookkeeping that was already dispatched records that result.\n- A failure of the channel never fails a write that committed.\n- After the context ends, no later step runs: no signer, session,\n  POST, proof or clearing of a slot. An act that began keeps its\n  unresolved custody. A signer that already ran is not undone.\n- An unreadable `find` keeps the join slot. An error is never an\n  unsigned absence.\n\nA refusal of a retired store uses the storage answer that custody\nhas today. When no existing answer fits, name the new one in an act\nbefore source.\n\nThe two store findings of afb50edf are in NF-5 and precede its\ngate. The hosted Counter half stays NF-7.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}